Description: Native interface to the spatial network analysis engine ('pstalgo') of the 'Place Syntax Tool' ('PST'), bundled at the pinned version 3.3.2. Axial (crossing-aware line) and endpoint-connected segment graphs are built once in native memory and reused for 'PST' network integration, reach, betweenness, angular, attraction, segment-group, isovist and raster analyses. Inputs can be numeric matrices, 'sf' objects or, with the suggested packages, 'GeoParquet' and 'FlatGeobuf' files. The package also bundles colour palettes (historical 'Axman' and 'Depthmap' colour modes, white-background adaptations and the Coral palettes, with optional 'ggplot2' scales) and a Barnsbury example network (axial map, unlinks and gate observations) adapted from Hillier and Iida (2005) <doi:10.1007/11556114_30>, with movement observations originally reported by Penn et al. (1998) <doi:10.1068/b250059>.License: LGPL (>= 3)
